From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:49:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: apple,s8000-vxd: Add the T8010 decoder

The Apple T8010 (A10) has the same Imagination MSVDX decoder family as
the S8000, reported as vxd-version 10 in the Apple device tree. It has a
second, 4 KiB register range that AppleD5500 calls the integration
registers.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml       | 28 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml
index 6cb5e83f4929..a6c1aebb78ff 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml
@@ -13,16 +13,21 @@ description:
   The Apple "VXD" block is a multi-standard hardware video decoder, an
   Imagination PowerVR MSVDX core whose MTX (META) microcontroller runs the
   DEVA firmware. Apple has used this IP family since the S5L8940X (A4); the
-  S8000/S8003 (A9) reports vxd-version 7 in the Apple device tree. The block
-  has no DART; it translates its own memory accesses through a two-level
+  S8000/S8003 (A9) reports vxd-version 7 in the Apple device tree, the T8010
+  (A10) vxd-version 10. The block has no DART; it translates its own memory accesses through a two-level
   "GART" that the host programs through the MTX MMU registers.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: apple,s8000-vxd
+    enum:
+      - apple,s8000-vxd
+      - apple,t8010-vxd
 
   reg:
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: decoder core registers
+      - description: second register range of the T8010 block
 
   interrupts:
     maxItems: 1
@@ -36,6 +41,21 @@ required:
   - interrupts
   - power-domains
 
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: apple,t8010-vxd
+    then:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          minItems: 2
+    else:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          maxItems: 1
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
